From fa2725c1cdee3f3995695cff52cbf3aa59628ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 15:10:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix: provision paying users reliably (sign up / payment /
 access)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of "pagué pero no puedo registrarme" and recurring access
failures: the Square webhook INSERT referenced columns the migrations never
created (square_customer_id, square_order_id, subscription_status,
payment_provider) and the schema had password_hash NOT NULL, while the
webhook provisions the user BEFORE they pick a password. Every new payment
made the INSERT throw, so the user row was never created and registration
was permanently blocked.

- Add migrations for the four Square columns and DROP NOT NULL on
  password_hash so the webhook can provision the account on payment.
- Robust buyer-email extraction for Square Payment Links: fetch the full
  order via the Orders API (email lives on the order's custom field, not on
  the payment event) and deep-scan any Square payload for an email.
- Log payments that arrive without an extractable email to error_logs
  instead of silently dropping them.
- Frontend: bound the "pago procesándose" polling (was an infinite loop)
  and show a clear, actionable message when access can't be confirmed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014YVy2mZxsEBHQoz3GyeNcd
